      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Augmented reality: a virtual cube on an ArUco marker board\n\n1. 'CV ArUco Detect Markers' finds every marker of the chosen dictionary (here DICT_6X6_250) and returns their image corners + ids. It is failure-tolerant: no markers -> count 0, empty arrays.\n2. 'CV ArUco Draw Markers' overlays the detected outlines and ids (visualization only).\n3. 'CV ArUco Board Pose (Average)' solves each marker's pose (IPPE_SQUARE) and AVERAGES them - rotation matrices meaned + re-orthonormalized (SVD), translations meaned to the board centroid. The planar pose flip is resolved per marker (normal facing the camera) so a stray marker cannot skew the mean. 'CV Camera Matrix' supplies approximate intrinsics (fx=fy=image width, principal point = image center). marker_length sets the world unit.\n4. A virtual cube ('CV Points', 3D, +z = up out of the board, centered on the centroid) is projected with cv2.projectPoints and drawn as a single polyline through its 12 edges ('Draw Polygon', open).\n5. Basic data handling 'if/else' gates the cube on 'found': without markers the marker overlay passes through unchanged.\n\nInspect the recovered board pose (rvec/tvec) as text."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
